# Pack-owned, so this rule reaches every existing project through a Pack Update.
# The root .gitignore is user-owned and frozen at init, and it can never carry a
# rule a later release needs (conflict C11 of #85).
#
# A forced update saves the pack-owned bytes it replaces here, one file per
# replaced path. The backups are recovery material for the owner of the project,
# they are never release content, and no guardrail scan reads them.
.drift/
